Durable Chunk Byte Staging (Cross-Instance Accessible):
Because arbitrary chunk sizes in /api/object-storage/upload-chunk are up to 2 MB (MAX_CHUNK_SIZE_BYTES = 2 * 1024 * 1024, whereas S3/R2 native UploadPart requires a 5 MB minimum part size for all non-final parts), each validated chunk i is durably written to a scoped staging key in the configured storage backend:
When r2 or s3_compatible is active: PUT to staging/${sessionId}/part-${String(chunkIndex).padStart(4, '0')}.bin in R2/S3 (with an R2 bucket lifecycle rule auto-expiring staging/ objects after 24 hours).
When local_bucket is active (development/test): written atomically to .object-storage-bucket/staging/${sessionId}/part-${chunkIndex}.bin (0o600).
This guarantees any Cloud Run instance can handle upload-init, upload-chunk, and upload-complete in any order and survive instance restarts.
Handling Every Failure & Edge Case:
Requests Reaching Different Cloud Run Instances / Instance Restart: Every handler loads and updates media_multipart_sessions_v2/{sessionId} via Firestore transaction and reads/writes chunk bytes from the shared staging/${sessionId}/ prefix.
Duplicate Chunk Requests (Idempotent Retry):
Compute sha256 = computeSha256Hex(buf).
If session.uploadedParts[chunkIndex] already exists:
If existingPart.sha256 === sha256 && existingPart.sizeBytes === buf.length: return 200 OK ({ status: 'ok', chunkIndex, receivedChunks: Object.keys(session.uploadedParts).length, idempotentReplay: true }).
If existingPart.sha256 !== sha256: return 409 DUPLICATE_CHUNK_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH (DUPLICATE_CHUNK_OVERWRITE_FORBIDDEN preserved for conflicting payload bytes).
Missing or Out-of-Order Chunks:
Chunks 0 .. totalChunks - 1 may arrive in any order or concurrently across instances; Firestore transaction updates uploadedParts.${chunkIndex} atomically and recalculates receivedBytes.
If upload-complete is called when Object.keys(session.uploadedParts).length < session.totalChunks or any index 0 .. totalChunks - 1 is missing, return 400 INCOMPLETE_CHUNKS with missingChunkIndices: number[], leaving the session in UPLOADING state so the client can upload only the missing chunks.
Upload Completion Retries & Concurrency:
If session.status === 'COMPLETED' and session.resultObjectId is set, POST /api/object-storage/upload-complete returns 200 OK with the already-registered mediaObject (idempotentReplay: true).
If session.status === 'COMPLETING' (another request is currently assembling), return 409 UPLOAD_COMPLETION_IN_PROGRESS (retryable).
Do not delete staging parts or mark the session ABORTED on transient remote write failure during upload-complete; revert status from COMPLETING to UPLOADING so the client can retry upload-complete without re-uploading chunks.
Abandoned Multipart Sessions:
Sessions past expiresAtIso (15 minutes) are transitioned to EXPIRED, and their staging/${sessionId}/part-*.bin objects are deleted by the durable cleanup job (MediaOrphanAndCleanupEngine).
Owner Authorization & Quota Enforcement:
upload-init, upload-chunk, and upload-complete require verified Firebase user authentication (verifyAuthenticatedUserHeader) and enforce session.ownerUid === userAuth.uid (403 UPLOAD_SESSION_OWNER_MISMATCH).
Active sessions per owner (status IN ['INITIATED', 'UPLOADING', 'COMPLETING'] and expiresAtIso > now) are capped at MAX_ACTIVE_CHUNK_SESSIONS_PER_USER = 2, global active sessions at MAX_ACTIVE_CHUNK_SESSIONS_TOTAL = 25, and cumulative receivedBytes + buf.length <= session.maxAllowedBytes and owner storage quota (MAX_OBJECTS_PER_OWNER = 30, MAX_BYTES_PER_OWNER = 500 MB).
