6.3 Channel-Specific Suppression, Quiet-Hour Calculation, Retry & Audit Behavior
Quiet-Hour Calculation (computeQuietHoursDeferredIso(nowIso, quietHoursUtc)):
Supports both same-day windows (startHourUtc < endHourUtc, e.g. 01:00..06:00 UTC) and overnight wrap-around windows (startHourUtc > endHourUtc, e.g. default 20:00..04:00 UTC = 23:30..07:30 Asia/Tehran).
When quietHoursUtc.enabled === true and categoryClass !== 'CRITICAL_TRANSACTIONAL', external delivery jobs (EMAIL, SMS, PUSH) remain QUEUED_OUTBOX / RETRY_SCHEDULED with nextAttemptAtIso set to the next occurrence of endHourUtc:00:00.000Z.
Pre-Dispatch Consent Re-Verification:
Because a user may revoke consent or enable globalOptOutAllNonCritical between Stage 2 (generateNotificationsFromOutbox) and Stage 3 (dispatchSingleDeliveryJob, especially after a retry backoff or quiet-hours deferral), dispatchSingleDeliveryJob (server/modules/notifications/notificationEngine.ts:367) must re-evaluate evaluateChannelEligibility() immediately before invoking dispatchThroughChannelAdapter(). If consent was revoked in the meantime, transition the job to SUPPRESSED_PREFERENCE_OR_CONSENT without calling the external provider.
Retry & Audit Trail:
Max attempts: DEFAULT_MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS = 3 with exponential backoff 30s * 2^(attempt - 1) (preferenceAndConsentService.ts:48-52), adjusted for quietHoursUtc.
Every suppression, deferral, preference/consent update, dispatch attempt, and receipt confirmation appends a RedactedOperationalLogEntry (hashRecipientUidForLog(uid) + redactPrivateContactDetails()) persisted to Firestore (notification_operational_logs_v2 / durable store).
