Produce a deterministic JSON/Markdown report classifying every discovered objectId / objectKey into:
RECONCILED_COMPLETE: Present in Firestore metadata + byte storage verified + checksum/size match.
LEGACY_INDEX_ONLY_NEEDS_FIRESTORE_BACKFILL: Present in .object-storage-bucket/index.json or legacy mediaObjects, missing in media_object_metadata_v2.
LOCAL_BYTES_ONLY_NEEDS_REMOTE_UPLOAD: remoteS3Synced === false or missing in remote bucket; bytes exist on local disk and must be uploaded to R2/S3 before switching provider.
METADATA_WITHOUT_BYTES_CORRUPT: Referenced in index.json, mediaObjects, media_object_metadata_v2, or bargains, but bytes do not exist on local disk or remote storage.
DANGLING_UNREFERENCED_BYTES: Bytes exist on disk or remote bucket with no metadata and no Bargain/Sponsor reference.
Go / No-Go Gate (Gate 0):
Storage provider cutover to r2 is blocked until LOCAL_BYTES_ONLY_NEEDS_REMOTE_UPLOAD === 0 and LEGACY_INDEX_ONLY_NEEDS_FIRESTORE_BACKFILL === 0.
